    theory: ['In this lab, we will delve into the more advanced details of traits that were previously covered in \'Traits: Defining Shared Behavior\', now that you have a better understanding of Rust. We first covered traits in "Traits: Defining Shared Behavior", but we didn\'t discuss the more advanced details. Now that you know more about Rust, we can get into the nitty-gritty. _Associated types_ connect a type placeholder with a trait such that the trait method definitions can use these placeholder types in their signatures. The implementor of a trait will specify the concrete type to be used instead of the placeholder type for the particular implementation. That way, we can define a trait that uses some types without needing to know exactly what those types are until the trait is implemented. Source: rust-lang/book · MIT.'],
